==Serbo-Croatian==

===Etymology===
{{suffix|sh|Srbija|nac|sc=Latn}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{sh-IPA|Srbijánac}}
* {{hyphenation|sh|Sr|bi|ja|nac}}

===Proper noun===
{{sh-noun|g=m|head=Srbijánac}}

# an inhabitant or a resident of region [[Serbia]]
# {{lb|sh|usually|Croatia|sometimes|derogatory}} a citizen of the country of [[Serbia]]

====Usage notes====
{{rfref|sh}}
The term {{m|sh|Sȑbin}} denotes an ethnic Serb, while the term {{m|sh|Srbijánac}} has a more specific meaning - a person from Republic of Serbia or Serbia proper. Since it is sometimes considered derogatory (especially in Serbia), the terms {{m|sh|Sȑbin}} and {{m|sh|Sȑpkinja}} should be used instead if possible.

